GNOME Shell doesn't expose the focused window to other programs, so Keysmith
ships a tiny extension that reports it over D-Bus (window.class / window.title).

Packages install it system-wide; enable it once per user:
  gnome-extensions enable keysmith@fagostini.github.io
On Wayland, log out and back in first if GNOME says the extension doesn't exist.

Manual install:
  cp -r keysmith@fagostini.github.io ~/.local/share/gnome-shell/extensions/
